It turns out that the getP() function, and by extension parboot(), was not properly handling missing values in the covariates for gdistsamp analyses. I've fixed this <https://github.com/rbchan/unmarked/commit/edff89387aa7f301c3c444a259f79017ec0fff52> in the dev version of unmarked on Github. Before this version makes it to CRAN, you can also fix this error by applying the patch I've attached to this email (gdistsamp_patch.R). To use the patch, completely restart R, load unmarked, and then source in the patch file with

source("gdistsamp_patch.R")

Thank you Nigel for helping me track this bug down!

Ken

